CVPR-2023-P0092,CVPR-2023-A000489,Jiarui Xu,shared,3,6,6,UC San Diego NVIDIA K-Means Clustering of Internal Diﬀusion Features Open-Vocabulary Panoptic Segmentation Prediction from ODISE Figure . We learn open-vocabulary panoptic segmentation with the internal representation of text-to-image diffusion models. K-Means clustering of the diffusion model’s internal representation shows semantically differentiated and localized information wherein objects are well grouped together (middle figure). We leverage these dense and rich diffusion features to perform open-vocabulary panoptic segmentation (right figure).,-6,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P0092.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Xu_Open-Vocabulary_Panoptic_Segmentation_With_Text-to-Image_Diffusion_Models_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
