CVPR-2023-P0590,CVPR-2023-A003072,Chun-Han Yao,shared,3,6,6,"UC Merced Skeleton discovery Google Research Yonsei University 3D shape or skeleton template … … Image ensemble Waymo Shared parts Instance parts Textured Input Instance parts Textured Figure . Hi-LASSIE overview and sample reconstructions. Given - images of an articulated animal class, we first discover a generic 3D skeleton, then jointly optimize the camera viewpoints, skeleton articulations, as well as shared and instance-specific neural part shapes. Hi-LASSIE is able to produce high-fidelity shapes and texture without any pre-defined shape model or 3D skeleton annotations. The part-based representation also allows applications like animation and motion re-targeting.",0,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P0590.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Yao_Hi-LASSIE_High-Fidelity_Articulated_Shape_and_Skeleton_Discovery_From_Sparse_Image_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
