CVPR-2023-P0773,CVPR-2023-A004026,Ron Mokady,shared,3,5,5,"Google Research The Blavatnik School of Computer Science, Tel Aviv University Input Image DDIM Inversion NULL-text Inversion Prompt-to-Prompt image editing Input caption: “Zoom photo of flowers.” “...origami flowers...” flowers Input caption: “A cat sitting next to a mirror.” “...silver cat sculpture...” cat cupcakes “...wither flowers...” tiger “...sleeping cat...” photo sketch “Watercolor drawing of...” Figure . Null-text inversion for real image editing. Our method takes as input a real image (leftmost column) and an associated caption. The image is inverted with a DDIM diffusion model to yield a diffusion trajectory (second column to the left). Once inverted, we use the initial trajectory as a pivot for null-text optimization that accurately reconstructs the input image (third column to the left). Then, we can edit the inverted image by modifying only the input caption using the editing technique of Prompt-to-Prompt [",-3,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P0773.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Mokady_NULL-Text_Inversion_for_Editing_Real_Images_Using_Guided_Diffusion_Models_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
