CVPR-2023-P0860,CVPR-2023-A004509,Antoine Yang,shared,3,8,8,"♯ Google Research DeepMind ¶ Inria Paris and Département d’informatique de l’ENS, CNRS, PSL Research University Czech Institute of Informatics, Robotics and Cybernetics at the Czech Technical University in Prague Large-scale pretraining from narrated videos Dense video captioning Vid2Seq Hey guys today I am going to teach you how to ski The kids make it look easy First slope, congratz! <1s><8s>The man is fastening the dog. <20s><50s>The dogs are pulling the sled. <45s><49s>The man is saying hello. Figure . Vid2Seq is a visual language model that predicts dense event captions together with their temporal grounding in the video by generating a single sequence of tokens (right). This ability is enabled by large-scale pretraining on unlabeled narrated videos (left).",-1,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P0860.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Yang_Vid2Seq_Large-Scale_Pretraining_of_a_Visual_Language_Model_for_Dense_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
