CVPR-2023-P0941,CVPR-2023-A004959,Dongyeun Lee,shared,3,6,6,"KAIST Klleon AI Research UNIST ℋ𝑠𝑠 ℋ𝑠𝑠→𝑡𝑡 𝐧𝐧𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎 Feature space ℋ 𝐧𝐧𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟 ℋ𝑡𝑡 Transfer Learning 𝐧𝐧𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎 Generated from Gs More Source Generated from Gs→t 𝐧𝐧𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟 More Target Figure . Given a source model Gs , our method can smoothly control the degree of source domain features in a fine-tuned model Gs→t . Samples in each row are generated from the same latent code z ∈ Z by Gs and Gs→t . Here, Hs , Hs→t , and Ht denote feature spaces of the source, our model, and simply fine-tuned target model, respectively. Our approach explicitly guides the model to preserve the source features by using the anchor point nanch , which allows a flexible and smooth cross-domain control via Gs→t .",-12,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P0941.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Lee_Fix_the_Noise_Disentangling_Source_Feature_for_Controllable_Domain_Translation_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
