CVPR-2023-P1234,CVPR-2023-A006583,Shubh Maheshwari,shared,3,3,3,"Indian Institute of Technology Delhi, India Figure . Transfer4D is an unsupervised technique for intra-category motion transfer from monocular depth videos (highlighted in the green box) to virtual characters of varying shapes (blue). It is category-agnostic, permitting motion transfer between quadrupeds (left), between bipeds (center and right), and in general between any characters with similar topology. Skeletons shown in yellow are extracted using our proposed unsupervised skeletonization algorithm. Please refer to the demo video on the project webpage: https: //transfer4d.github.io/ and Fig. for diverse animation sequences ranging bipeds and quadrupeds.",0,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P1234.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Maheshwari_Transfer4D_A_Framework_for_Frugal_Motion_Capture_and_Deformation_Transfer_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
