CVPR-2023-P1344,CVPR-2023-A007165,Xiaoshuai Zhang,shared,3,6,6,"Google Research Stanford University University of California, San Diego Figure . We propose to represent the scene with a set of local neural radiance fields, named nerflets, which are trained with only 2D supervision. Our representation is not only useful for 2D tasks such as novel view synthesis and panoptic segmentation, but also capable of solving 3D-oriented tasks such as 3D segmentation and scene editing. The key idea is our learned structured decomposition (top right).",-3,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P1344.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Zhang_Nerflets_Local_Radiance_Fields_for_Efficient_Structure-Aware_3D_Scene_Representation_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
