CVPR-2023-P1381,CVPR-2023-A007374,Lin Huang,shared,3,7,7,"University at Buffalo Microsoft RGB input 3D hand mesh Wrist Thumb root Index tip Middle root Ring tip Pinky root 3D hand pose (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) (f) (g) (h) (i) Figure . We present Neural Voting Field (NVF), a 3D implicit function for camera-space 3D hand pose estimation from an RGB image. Given an RGB input (a), for a 3D point in camera space, NVF can predict its signed distance to hand surface and a set of 4D offset vectors (1D voting weight and 3D directional vector to each joint). 3D pose is then obtained via dense 3D point-wise voting. Rendered predictions: (b) Hand mesh generated by Marching Cubes from the predicted signed distances (c-h) Predicted 1D voting weight from each predicted near-surface 3D point to a joint. (Brighter line means larger weight, darker or no line means smaller weight) (i) Estimated 3D hand pose.",-2,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P1381.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Huang_Neural_Voting_Field_for_Camera-Space_3D_Hand_Pose_Estimation_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
