CVPR-2023-P1979,CVPR-2023-A010564,Xiaosong Jia,shared,3,7,7,"Shanghai Jiao Tong University Shanghai AI Laboratory University of California at San Diego Correspondence authors Throttle . Steer . Adjust Driving Plan Look OK to Follow Better to be Faster Oncoming car yields Predict Throttle++ Steer++ × 𝑵𝑵 Figure . We propose ThinkTwice, a scalable decoder paradigm that generates the future trajectory and action of the ego vehicle sfor end-to-end autonomous driving. Conditioned on the coarse action/trajectory, we propose the Look Module to retrieve information from critical regions and the Prediction Module to anticipate the outcome of the ego behavior. Taking features from the two modules as input, the coarse prediction is refined by predicting its offset from ground-truth. We could stack multiple such layers and scale up the capacity of the decoder with dense supervision and spatial-temporal prior.",-5,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P1979.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Jia_Think_Twice_Before_Driving_Towards_Scalable_Decoders_for_End-to-End_Autonomous_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
