CVPR-2023-P2196,CVPR-2023-A011903,Jie Qin,shared,3,11,11,"Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences ByteDance Inc School of Artificial Intelligence, University of Chinese Academy of Sciences Seen Class Class2 Class1 … Classn Task: Semantic Adaptive Class Prompt All-in-one FreeSeg Adaptive Task Prompt Task: Semantic Task: Instance Task: Panoptic Unseen Class FreeSeg Semantic mIoU-Unseen (ADE) Semantic mIoU-Seen (ADE) Semantic mIoU-Unseen (VOC) Semantic mIoU-Seen (VOC) Semantic mIoU-Unseen (COCO) Instance mAP-Seen (ADE) sharing Seen Class: 'person', 'car’, 'traffic light’, 'building' Task: Instance Instance mAP-Unseen (ADE) FreeSeg Instance mAP-Seen (COCO) sharing Unseen Class: 'skateboard', 'road', 'tree’ (a) One-shot Training Task: Panoptic Semantic mIoU-Seen (COCO) Instance mAP-Unseen (COCO) FreeSeg (b) Multi-task Inference Panoptic PQ-Unseen (ADE) Panoptic PQ-Seen (COCO) Panoptic PQ-Unseen (COCO) Panoptic PQ-Seen (ADE) (c) Performance Diagram Figure . We propose FreeSeg, a generic framework to accomplish Unified, Universal and Open-Vocabulary Image Segmentation. (a) FreeSeg optimizes an all-in-one network via one-shot training. (b) FreeSeg employs the same architecture and parameters to handle diverse segmentation tasks seamlessly in the inference procedure. (c) FreeSeg establishes new state-of-the-art performance across diverse segmentation tasks, training datasets and zero-shot generalization.",1,data/raw/cvpr/2023/first_pages/CVPR-2023-P2196.txt,https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023/papers/Qin_FreeSeg_Unified_Universal_and_Open-Vocabulary_Image_Segmentation_CVPR_2023_paper.pdf
